"Functional test fixes for the Waldorf community task manager (Hungarian UI), on branch feature/functional-test-fixes. Exploratory test pass findings. Fix: (1) Opening a notification keeps the parent in the Értesítések section: menu highlights Értesítések and the back link goes back to the notifications list (Vissza az értesítésekhez). (2) Opening a notification marks it read; returning to the list shows it read; checkbox keeps working. (3) Read notifications are greyed out as a whole card (muted, WCAG contrast 4.5:1 kept). (4) Értesítések is the FIRST parent menu item before Feladatok; the parent default page stays Értesítések. (5) Admin detail pages (records, tasks and events, approvals, archive) and the two new forms get a visible back link to their list. (6) The status filter only offers statuses that apply to that list (approvals: Függőben, Jóváhagyva and other real values; records: Aktív, Archivált; tasks: real task statuses), approved requests become filterable, existing filter links keep working. (7) Parent swap and cancel requests: clear confirmation after submit, no duplicate submit, the task detail shows the pending request state and no longer offers the same request. (8) Remove e2e test leftovers (Firefox próba, mobil próba) from user-visible demo data if tests do not need them, and hide technical text from normal screens: correlation id on Emlékeztetők, test-scenario selectors on task details, Verzió: 1 (keep only behind a marked developer section if tests need them). (9) Empty Új rekord and Új feladat vagy esemény submit shows a clear Hungarian validation message. Keep the design, accessibility, responsive layout, update and extend tests including Playwright journey specs for the notification journey, and update the user guide."
